
==========================================================================
  Zn CONTROLLED PHASE ROTATION E2E DEMO
==========================================================================

Coherent control over cyclic groups via Linear DSL


==========================================================================
  PART 1: Datatype Declarations
==========================================================================
  Z2: arity=2, 1 tag qubits
  Z4: arity=4, 2 tag qubits
  Z5: arity=5, 3 tag qubits
  Z8: arity=8, 3 tag qubits

==========================================================================
  PART 2: Z2 Controlled Phase
==========================================================================

  control z2 q [| id q; gate_z |]
  Branch 0: identity, Branch 1: Z gate


Z2 phase: Z2 ⊗ Q → Z2 ⊗ Q:
2 qubits, 1 gates
  CZ q[0, 1]
  perm: [0, 1]

==========================================================================
  PART 3: Z4 Controlled Phase
==========================================================================

  control z4 q [| Rz(0); Rz(0.5); Rz(1.0); Rz(1.5) |]  (half-turns)
  Branch k: Rz(k/2) half-turns = e^{ikπ/2} relative phase


Z4 phase: Z4 ⊗ Q → Z4 ⊗ Q:
3 qubits, 12 gates
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[0]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2]
  X q[1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2]
  perm: [0, 1, 2]

==========================================================================
  PART 4: Z5 Controlled Phase
==========================================================================

  control z5 q [| Rz(0); Rz(2/5); Rz(4/5); Rz(6/5); Rz(8/5) |]  (half-turns)
  Branch k: Rz(2k/5) half-turns = e^{i2πk/5} relative phase


Z5 phase: Z5 ⊗ Q → Z5 ⊗ Q:
4 qubits, 25 gates
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  X q[0]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[2]
  X q[0]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  perm: [0, 1, 2, 3]

==========================================================================
  PART 5: Z8 Controlled Phase
==========================================================================

  control z8 q [| Rz(0); Rz(0.25); ...; Rz(1.75) |]  (half-turns)
  Branch k: Rz(k/4) half-turns = e^{ikπ/4} relative phase


Z8 phase: Z8 ⊗ Q → Z8 ⊗ Q:
4 qubits, 32 gates
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  X q[0]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[2]
  X q[0]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  X q[1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[1]
  X q[2]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[2]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  perm: [0, 1, 2, 3]

==========================================================================
  PART 6: Semantic Verification
==========================================================================

Verifying correctness: control with forward phases composed with
inverse phases should give identity (f ; f^{-1} = id).

  ✓ Z2: phase ; phase^{-1} = id (fidelity=1.000000)
  ✓ Z4: phase ; phase^{-1} = id (fidelity=1.000000)
  ✓ Z5: phase ; phase^{-1} = id (fidelity=1.000000)
  ✓ Z8: phase ; phase^{-1} = id (fidelity=1.000000)
  ✓ Z4: control [id;id;id;id] = id (trivial) (fidelity=1.000000)
  ✓ Z8: control [id;...;id] = id (trivial) (fidelity=1.000000)

Verification: 6/6 passed

==========================================================================
  SUMMARY
==========================================================================

Compiled Zn controlled phase rotations via Linear DSL:

  Z2: control z2 q [id; Z]           1 tag qubits
  Z4: control z4 q [Rz(k/2)]         2 tag qubits
  Z5: control z5 q [Rz(2k/5)]        3 tag qubits
  Z8: control z8 q [Rz(k/4)]         3 tag qubits

All use the `control` combinator on declared datatypes.
The compiler handles tag encoding and multi-controlled gates.

